      "event": "ac-updated",
      "detail": "The shell's own makeProvider returns an empty FakeProvider when a provider has no credential; keryx acp discards it at once and reports the provider unconfigured. Avoiding the construction itself would mean copying makeProvider's credential logic, which the first half of this criterion forbids. The property the operator needs — no turn ever runs against a fake — is what is now asserted."
